1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,833
Recourse: receipts for welfare algorithms.

2
00:00:03,883 --> 00:00:10,226
I'm Jannet Akanksha Ekka, and this is my
Tech Track entry for Web3 for Social Good.

3
00:00:10,276 --> 00:00:15,589
In Telangana, an automated system
decides who keeps subsidised food.

4
00:00:15,639 --> 00:00:20,542
A match across government databases
removes the family from the scheme.

5
00:00:20,592 --> 00:00:25,922
In 2024, Al Jazeera reported that it
tagged Bismillah Bee's late husband,

6
00:00:25,972 --> 00:00:30,860
a rickshaw puller, as a car owner,
and her family lost its rations.

7
00:00:30,910 --> 00:00:35,954
About twenty lakh ration cards
were deleted from 2016 on.

8
00:00:36,004 --> 00:00:39,209
The family can't see which record did it.

9
00:00:39,259 --> 00:00:43,089
Nobody outside the department
can check which rules ran,

10
00:00:43,139 --> 00:00:44,751
or whether they changed.

11
00:00:44,801 --> 00:00:49,466
The department keeps the only log,
and it is the party being checked.

12
00:00:49,516 --> 00:00:52,282
Recourse is built for three people.

13
00:00:52,332 --> 00:00:56,326
The family, who needs to
know what decided their case.

14
00:00:56,376 --> 00:00:59,723
The legal-aid worker, who files the appeal.

15
00:00:59,773 --> 00:01:05,124
And the auditor or journalist, who needs
to see how often the system gets it wrong.

16
00:01:05,174 --> 00:01:08,863
It does four things: rules
on chain before they're used,

17
00:01:08,913 --> 00:01:12,069
a receipt with only the
records that decided it,

18
00:01:12,119 --> 00:01:16,922
an explanation in the family's own
language, and appeals on the record.

19
00:01:16,972 --> 00:01:19,301
Here is the architecture.

20
00:01:19,351 --> 00:01:22,874
Decisions stay in the agency's own system.

21
00:01:22,924 --> 00:01:26,755
The engine matches every
household against the vehicle,

22
00:01:26,805 --> 00:01:31,271
income tax and payroll registries,
under a published rules file.

23
00:01:31,321 --> 00:01:35,074
Each decision becomes a
salted receipt, and its hash,

24
00:01:35,124 --> 00:01:38,806
joined with the outcome,
is a leaf in a Merkle tree.

25
00:01:38,856 --> 00:01:44,909
From the agency's system, only two things
go on chain: the hash of each rules file,

26
00:01:44,959 --> 00:01:46,601
and one root per batch.

27
00:01:46,651 --> 00:01:50,646
The Recourse contract on
Monad testnet has no owner.

28
00:01:50,696 --> 00:01:55,976
It holds the rule versions, the batch
roots, the appeals and the answers.

29
00:01:56,026 --> 00:02:01,336
The family keeps the receipt, and their
browser checks it against the contract

30
00:02:01,386 --> 00:02:02,066
directly.

31
00:02:02,116 --> 00:02:05,117
Three design choices keep it honest.

32
00:02:05,167 --> 00:02:09,033
No personal data goes on chain, only hashes.

33
00:02:09,083 --> 00:02:13,558
A record counts as a reason only
if removing it changes the outcome,

34
00:02:13,608 --> 00:02:17,617
so a refusal can't be padded
with records that didn't matter.

35
00:02:17,667 --> 00:02:20,683
And Gemini only rewords the receipt.

36
00:02:20,733 --> 00:02:24,333
A guard checks every number
and record ID it writes,

37
00:02:24,383 --> 00:02:29,642
and throws out any draft that invents
one or leaves out a decisive record.

38
00:02:29,692 --> 00:02:33,849
Here is the working prototype,
live on Monad testnet.

39
00:02:33,899 --> 00:02:37,835
Amina is invented, and
modelled on Bismillah Bee.

40
00:02:37,885 --> 00:02:41,252
Her family was refused under
version two of the rules,

41
00:02:41,302 --> 00:02:44,226
and version one would
have found them eligible.

42
00:02:44,276 --> 00:02:51,243
One record decided it: a Toyota Innova,
registered in 2022 in Banjara Hills.

43
00:02:51,293 --> 00:02:56,632
Her husband died in 2019, and
the family lives in Falaknuma.

44
00:02:56,682 --> 00:03:00,026
The match sat exactly at the threshold.

45
00:03:00,076 --> 00:03:04,418
She can read the same receipt
in Telugu, or in Hindi.

46
00:03:04,468 --> 00:03:08,427
Her browser checks the receipt
against the chain: its hash,

47
00:03:08,477 --> 00:03:13,727
its Merkle proof, the published rules
file, and that the rules came before the

48
00:03:13,777 --> 00:03:14,085
batch.

49
00:03:14,135 --> 00:03:17,810
Change one fact, and every check fails.

50
00:03:17,860 --> 00:03:23,255
A legal-aid worker filed her appeal on
chain, with a letter Gemini drafted.

51
00:03:23,305 --> 00:03:26,392
The agency's answer is sealed too.

52
00:03:26,442 --> 00:03:28,490
Decision reversed.

53
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:33,145
Anyone can open the public record,
read live from the contract.

54
00:03:33,195 --> 00:03:38,469
When the agency switched to version two,
refusals went from seventy five households

55
00:03:38,519 --> 00:03:40,008
to two hundred and nine.

56
00:03:40,058 --> 00:03:45,339
Under version two, ten of the twelve
appeals the agency answered were reversed.

57
00:03:45,389 --> 00:03:50,090
Two are still waiting, and they go
overdue on the twentieth of November.

58
00:03:50,140 --> 00:03:51,703
What's new?

59
00:03:51,753 --> 00:03:54,939
A quiet rule change becomes
a public, dated event,

60
00:03:54,989 --> 00:04:00,052
and each receipt says whether the earlier
rules would have decided differently.

61
00:04:00,102 --> 00:04:03,071
Reasons are tested, not listed.

62
00:04:03,121 --> 00:04:07,387
That flip test comes from
my trading agent, SMT.

63
00:04:07,437 --> 00:04:11,196
The AI explains, but it can't add facts.

64
00:04:11,246 --> 00:04:15,506
And a missing answer is visible
to everyone, with a date.

65
00:04:15,556 --> 00:04:20,869
The impact is for families who lose food
through a database match they can't see.

66
00:04:20,919 --> 00:04:24,469
In the demo, version two caught
seventeen more real cases,

67
00:04:24,519 --> 00:04:28,069
and wrongly cut off a hundred
and seventeen more families,

68
00:04:28,119 --> 00:04:30,055
and the appeal outcomes show it.

69
00:04:30,105 --> 00:04:32,131
It's cheap to adopt.

70
00:04:32,181 --> 00:04:37,584
The agency seals each batch, about a hundred
and sixty thousand gas for a thousand

71
00:04:37,634 --> 00:04:40,444
decisions, and publishes each rule version.

72
00:04:40,494 --> 00:04:46,069
A pilot can start with a legal-aid group
that already files ration card appeals.

73
00:04:46,119 --> 00:04:49,467
Next, I'd load a real
state's published criteria,

74
00:04:49,517 --> 00:04:54,736
add spoken explanations, and give
auditors a tool to re-run the rules on any

75
00:04:54,786 --> 00:04:55,394
receipt.

76
00:04:55,444 --> 00:04:56,889
Recourse.

77
00:04:56,939 --> 00:05:02,728
The rules are public before they're used,
and every family can see what decided its

78
00:05:02,778 --> 00:05:03,080
case.

79
00:05:03,130 --> 00:05:04,582
Thank you.
